Subject: [C2] Enable the trusted compiled routed-MoE region on the LLM qwen3_5_moe path

`Qwen4ExpCompiledRoutedSwitchGLU` (SwitchLayers.swift:64-142) fuses all three
routed `gatherQuantizedMM` calls plus silu and multiply into ONE compiled
region. It is enabled by env default (`VMLX_QWEN4_EXP_COMPILE_ROUTED_MOE=1`)
and built with `vmlxTrustedCompile`, so it compiles WITHOUT the
`VMLX_ENABLE_UNSAFE_COMPILE` opt-in (Transforms+Compile.swift:301-318).

It is reached only when `SwitchGLU.compileSeparatedDecode == true`
(SwitchLayers.swift:400). That property defaults false and is passed true in
exactly one place in the tree — MLXVLM/Models/Qwen35.swift:2184, the VLM twin.
The LLM construction site that Ornith actually loads through omits it, so the
region has never executed for LLM-path qwen3_5_moe bundles.

--- a/Libraries/MLXLLM/Models/Qwen35.swift
+++ b/Libraries/MLXLLM/Models/Qwen35.swift
@@ -868,7 +868,8 @@
         _switchMLP.wrappedValue = SwitchGLU(
             inputDims: args.hiddenSize,
             hiddenDims: args.moeIntermediateSize,
-            numExperts: args.numExperts
+            numExperts: args.numExperts,
+            compileSeparatedDecode: true
         )
